                <pb facs="0860" n="748" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg748"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48/1050: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Viborg</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Imbrie</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Viborg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-15"><hi rendition="#italic">December 15,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 16, 5:51 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>165. Yudenitch requests that Viborg
                    stores with exception of 4,000 tons, about one week’s supply for Petrograd, be
                    sent Reval at once as his army and refugees in great distress. Last of American
                    Relief at Reval confirms need of food and advises sending Viborg stores, also
                    states that no American Relief stores expected at Reval.</p>
                <p>Request immediate instructions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Imbrie</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
